# GenTopo for slc10, so the EPN has its topology-generation scripts on el10.
# It has never been built for slc10 -- TARS/slc10_x86-64/GenTopo/ is empty,
# while slc9 has seven builds, the last nightly-20260121 -- so this exists to
# produce it rather than to release it repeatedly.
#
# A seconds-long build: the recipe only copies O2DPG/DATA/tools/epn/* and runs
# alibuild-generate-module, it has no runtime dependencies at all, and its one
# build dependency (alibuild-recipe-tools) is already in the CAS from the slc10
# PR builds, so it downloads rather than builds.
#
# The tag is cut on alidist, NOT on O2DPG, even though the version is an O2DPG
# nightly tag: the recipe pins `tag:` and `version: %(tag_basename)s` copies it,
# so which O2DPG nightly gets built is decided by alidist's content. One commit
# does both halves:
#   sed -i 's/^tag: .*/tag: "nightly-20261015"/' gentopo.sh   # an O2DPG tag
#   git commit -am 'GenTopo: nightly-20261015' && git push
#   git tag GenTopo-20261015 && git push origin GenTopo-20261015
# Keep the nightly-YYYYMMDD shape: aliPublish-s3-updatable-rpms.conf includes
# GenTopo on ^nightly-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]+$ and will skip anything else.
CI_NAME=build_GenTopo_slc10
PACKAGE=GenTopo
PR_REPO=alisw/alidist
PR_BRANCH=master
# Same defaults as the slc10 PR checks, so alibuild-recipe-tools is a store hit.
ALIBUILD_DEFAULTS=o2
# %(date) is required by list-release-tags -- without it the regex would match
# every tag of this shape ever cut, and alidist carries >10000 tags. The date is
# the day the build is wanted, not the O2DPG nightly; the version comes from the
# recipe. The leading literal "GenTopo-" is what GitHub filters on.
TAG_REGEX='^GenTopo-%(date)(?P<variant>-[0-9]{4})?$'
CHECK_NAME=release/GenTopo/slc10-x86
# Today and yesterday. The tag is cut by hand, so a worker that was busy or down
# when it landed should still pick it up; the tag's GitHub status stops it being
# built twice.
RELEASE_LOOKBACK_DAYS=1
DONT_USE_COMMENTS=1

# REBUILD_TAGS deliberately NOT set. Set it to this tag's name, temporarily, to
# re-run one that is already green -- cheap, because the tarball comes back out
# of the store.
